blocks.help.for = Counts with a variable from the first number to the last, running the blocks inside each time.
blocks.help.for_in = Runs the blocks inside once for each item of a list or table.
blocks.help.local = Makes a new variable: a name that holds a value. It only exists in this part of the script (local).
blocks.help.set = Changes the value of a variable (or a field of a table) that already exists.
blocks.help.change = Changes a variable using its current value.
blocks.help.function = Defines a function: a named group of blocks that other places run with "Run". The inputs are values it gets each time.
blocks.help.return_function = The whole file gives back this function: whoever loads it (like the Procedural Character) runs it.
blocks.help.return = Ends the function here and gives back a value (if any).
blocks.help.break = Leaves the loop it is in right away.
blocks.help.continue = Skips the rest of this round of the loop and goes on with the next one.
blocks.help.do = Groups blocks so their variables only exist inside.
blocks.help.call_api = An engine command. The values in white are what you give it; round blocks inside them are values the engine works out first.
blocks.help.call_user = Runs a function made in a script (this one or another).
blocks.help.code = Code that has no block yet. It is shown as written; edit it in Code.
blocks.help.comment = A note for people reading the script. It does nothing when the game runs.
blocks.help.reporter = A value block: the engine works it out right when the block around it runs.
